<title>FRANCE: SOCCER-PATHS OF NICE AND GUINGAMP TO THE FRENCH CUP FINAL.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PATHS OF NICE AND GUINGAMP TO THE FRENCH CUP FINAL.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the paths followed by Nice and Guingamp on their way to Saturday's French Cup Final at Parc des Princes (goal-scorers in parentheses, Roman numerals denote non-championship sides):</p>
<p>Nice (winners in 1952, 1954, finalists 1978)</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p> Valence (II)   0  Nice	    1 (De Neef)</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p> Bastia	   2  Nice	    2 (De Neef, Savini)</p>
<p>(after extra time, 2-2 at 90 mins, Nice won 4-3 on penalties)</p>
<p>Third round</p>
<p> Nice	     2  Guegnon (II)  0 (Debbah, Kubica)</p>
<p>Quarter-finals</p>
<p> Clermont (IV)  1  Nice	    2 (Debbah, Fugen)</p>
<p>(after extra time, 1-1 after 90 mins)</p>
<p>Semifinals</p>
<p> Laval (II)     0  Nice	    1 (De Neef)</p>
<p>- - - -</p>
<p>Guingamp (first final)</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p> Mont-de-Marsan (III) 0   Guingamp 1 (Wreh)</p>
<p>(after extra time)</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p> Wasquehal (III)	1   Guingamp 3 (Coridon, Horlaville, Wreh)</p>
<p>Third round</p>
<p> Guingamp		 1   Caen     0 (Coridon)</p>
<p>Quarter-finals</p>
<p> Creteil (III)   1   Guingamp 3 (Carnot, Coridon, Haon own goal)</p>
<p>(after extra time, 1-1 after 90 mins)</p>
<p>Semifinals</p>
<p> Guingamp	  2   Montpellier   0 (Wreh, Carnot)</p>
<p>(after extra time)</p>
</text>
